      "target_job": {
        "description": "Full-Stack Software Engineer (AI/ML Products)\nTechNova Solutions — Bangalore, India (Hybrid) — Full-time\n\nAbout the role\nWe're looking for a Full-Stack Software Engineer to join our product engineering team building AI-powered SaaS tools. You'll work across the stack — from React/Next.js frontends to Node.js/Express APIs — and collaborate closely with our ML team to ship features that put machine learning models in front of real users.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nDesign and build responsive, production-grade web applications using React, Next.js, and TypeScript\nDevelop and maintain RESTful APIs using Node.js and Express, with PostgreSQL as the primary data store\nIntegrate third-party AI APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, or similar) into product features\nOwn features end-to-end: from database schema design through deployment and monitoring\nWrite clean, tested code and participate in code reviews\nCollaborate with designers and product managers to translate requirements into technical specs\nOptimize application performance and ensure responsive design across devices\nImplement authentication, authorization, and data validation following security best practices\nDeploy and maintain CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions and Vercel/AWS\n\nRequirements\n\n1–3 years of professional experience in full-stack web development\nStrong proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, React, and modern frontend tooling (Vite, Tailwind CSS)\nExperience with Node.js, Express, and RESTful API design\nWorking knowledge of SQL databases (PostgreSQL preferred) and schema design\nFamiliarity with cloud storage (S3 or equivalent) and deployment platforms (Vercel, AWS, or GCP)\nUnderstanding of authentication patterns (JWT, OAuth) and basic security practices (input validation, XSS/CSRF prevention)\nExperience with Git, CI/CD pipelines, and agile development workflows\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or related field (or equivalent practical experience)\n\nNice to have\n\nExperience integrating LLM APIs into production applications\nExposure to data validation libraries (Zod, Yup)\nFamiliarity with animation libraries (GSAP, Framer Motion) for polished UI\nExperience with automated testing (Jest, Playwright)\nPrior work on a project involving document parsing or data extraction (PDF/DOCX)",
